  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1158 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nUnseasonably hot temperatures will prevail for much of the\nupcoming week. Generally dry weather will prevail the next few\ndays, but an isolated shower or thunderstorm cannot be totally\nruled out with the upper ridge centered just to our east. Recent\nrainfall will likely keep northern parts of the forecast area\nslightly below 100 degrees most days, with more southern areas\nthat have seen less rainfall seeing several more days of triple \ndigit heat. Afternoon heat index values will reach or exceed 105\ndegrees across much of eastern Oklahoma and west central Arkansas\nover the next several days. Increasing south winds Monday and\nTuesday will result in a limited fire weather danger despite\nrecent rainfall.\n\nThe upper ridge will eventually break down by next weekend\nallowing a cold front to move across the area. The timing of just\nwhen this occurs remains uncertain, with the latest model data \ndelaying the arrival of the front somewhat. Increasing rain \nchances and cooler temperatures will occur once the front arrives \nin a week or so.",
